  "description": "1.6.1.0 plus n°27: every packed SysEx message the machine sends (sound 60, beat 5F, project 5E and 5C n, files 63, 62 and 61) ends with its last partial group in the standard DSI layout (head bit j = MSB of data byte j, zero padding), the layout the machine's own receivers read; the factory flush shifted the head bits, left stale padding bytes and wrote one byte past its buffer. Voice, Panel and SAM unchanged.",
